WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.300
Design first: a career by design, not by first offer.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:09.860
Friday. Yoga opens his inbox and finds a job offer. His first. He is about to accept. Not because it fits, but because it came first.

3
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:15.460
One question stops him. Whose script is this line from?

4
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:23.880
Without a design, three scripts compete to run a career. The inheritance script: what the family respects. The feed script: whatever is trending. And the first-offer script: whoever says yes first.

5
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:32.590
So he designs first. His first mission sentence names a title. A title is not a direction. The rewrite names a contribution: I help small businesses understand their own numbers.

6
00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:41.460
A mission is a compass. It needs a first landmark: one outcome, three years out, with four parts. A domain, a level, evidence someone else can see, and a line you refuse to cross.

7
00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:48.970
On Monday he answers the offer with two questions. Will I work with small clients? Who will I learn from?

8
00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:55.930
He may still say yes. But now the yes is his: direction by design, not by first offer.

9
00:00:56.330 --> 00:01:03.330
A mission names contribution, not titles. A three-year outcome makes it plannable.

10
00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:08.130
Now it is your turn. For one big choice you face, ask: whose script is this line from?
